Input: {"question": "Who is the composer of Symphony No. 38?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 0, "end": 12, "text": "Symphony No."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 13, "end": 40, "text": "38 (Haydn) The Symphony No."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 41, "end": 119, "text": "38 in C major, Hoboken I/38, is an early and festive symphony by Joseph Haydn."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 120, "end": 178, "text": "The symphony was composed some time between 1765 and 1769."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 179, "end": 383, "text": "Because of the virtuosic oboe parts in the final two movements, it has been suggested that the work's composition may have coincided with the employ of the oboist Vittorino Colombazzo in the fall of 1768."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 384, "end": 528, "text": "The symphony is popularly called the Echo Symphony, a nickname that, like all other named Haydn symphonies, did not originate with the composer."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d00", "start": 529, "end": 587, "text": "It is typically referred to as the \"Echo\" Symphony because"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d01", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "Joseph Haydn Hob ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d01", "start": 19, "end": 23, "text": "No ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0308-7de6d8f07d1d:d01", "start": 24, "end": 557, "text": "[ 1 ] Title Key Date Instrumentation Notes XXVIII:1 Acide e Galatea C major 1763 SSATB , orchestra 1 act XXVIII:2 La canterina 1766 SSST , orchestra 2 acts XXVIII:3 Lo speziale G major 1768 SSTT , o